{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937794-what-s-the-mana-mileage-on-that","id":937794,"title":"What's the Mana mileage on that?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-26T15:19:55-07:00","id":937794,"title":"What's the Mana mileage on that?","content":"The recent errata published brought one idea to mind ... Platonic Ferrari! (or whatever other +Social car is prototypical in your head ... a Manawagen XD )<br /> <br /> As a Rote, with 1 Reach for Advanced Duration and 2 for the complex device, you do a nice long ritual to make yourself a glowy perfect dreamcar. You throw some potency around, give it a nice Mana tank capacity, fill it up with some Mana, and take it out for a spin!<br /> Ignoring for a moment the Sleepers dispelling your shiny new ride ( you drive in the middle of nowhere, like all those car commercials XD ) , how much mileage do you think a single point of Mana would get you?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T15:56:02-07:00","id":937812,"title":"","content":"Potentially infinite. You would deplete mana tank only when making Drive rolls, and you make Drive rolls only when going Too Fast Too Furious. For everyday driving, it could last forever.<br /> <br /> Of course, the temptation of going Too Fast Too Prime with such a cool car would be appropriate to the possible bonus...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:47:52-07:00","id":938246,"title":"","content":"&lt;Insert grating, but somehow obligatory, warning about Wisdom&gt;<br /> <br /> A swanky ride perfected reasonably still requires fuel or continuous creation of energy. Of course, playing such songs on repeat is quite doable in the new system. (Huh, <b>Create Energy</b> costs <i>nothing</i>. That makes this cheaper.) If Forces is your desired approach, make the vehicle entirely electrical and repeatedly charge the thing with an indefinite spell. Be sure to include the solar panels so to avoid pesky gremlins caused by Disbelief.<br /> <br /> Really regenerative braking: <b>Transform Energy</b> --- Kinetic(whole car &amp; contents) to Electricity(battery) when brake is lowered to the floor. (Since the momentum is translated into electricity, this shouldn't knock passengers around. It could get hard to believe, though.)<br /> <br /> A more conventional approach would use Matter. A CO_2 scrubber that translates the gas into a liquid fertilizer could take care of emissions and translating waste into fuel is certainly on Matter's can-do list. To be believable, you'd probably simply want to sequester the stuff. Spinning waste Co_2 into high-quality carbon fiber chains would be spiffy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T01:46:10-07:00","id":940539,"title":"","content":"Good points from both of you, thanks. Not sure why I thought it would run on the mana used.<br /> <br /> Back to my idle curiosity problem: Same scenario but we add Forces to the spell for the energy-transforming effect of using the mana tank inherent in the spell as fuel.<br /> <br /> Would one point of Mana be more or less a full tank of gas in a unit-to-unit sort of way, or are there other transformation considerations?<br /> <br /> Also ...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937794-what-s-the-mana-mileage-on-that?p=938246#post938246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;Insert grating, but somehow obligatory, warning about Wisdom&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Do all fun things risk Wisdom? Conversely, mages who use magic for funsies would advance faster than their wiser contemporaries. XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","user":"Aeryes","date":".  ergh, typos 07-31-2016, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:42:38-07:00","id":946576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937794-what-s-the-mana-mileage-on-that?p=940539#post940539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do all fun things risk Wisdom? Conversely, mages who use magic for funsies would advance faster than their wiser contemporaries. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Always.<br /> Until you're a Prelate.<br /> <br /> (This is how the Seers, Free Council, <i>and</i> Silver Ladder get willing recruits.)<br /> <br /> The mana to content ratio would actually hinge on the spell potency. There is no limited exchange rate.<br /> If you somehow got a ludicrous die pool, you could make enough energy to set off a sun. Mana is simply the cost of redefining reality and not related to the resulting energy state within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}